WEBVTT

00:00:00.685 --> 00:00:03.857
Tutorial six. Run, preview and save.

00:00:08.178 --> 00:00:16.226
Before you run, the Run tab lists how the numbers will be computed and shown. The workbook's Manifest sheet records the same settings.

00:00:16.526 --> 00:00:21.091
Tick Preview only, if you want to look at the results before anything is saved.

00:00:23.816 --> 00:00:30.703
Press Run. The log lists every step as it happens: filters, conversions, tests and figures.

00:00:30.983 --> 00:00:35.223
A full run takes a minute or two. It is shown here speeded up.

00:00:35.687 --> 00:00:38.395
Done. The workbook and the figures are ready.

00:00:38.609 --> 00:00:45.589
Previews of the figures appear in the app. Each figure is also written as its own file, with a legend file beside it.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:50.296
Here is the combined figure, with every panel and every group.

00:00:51.456 --> 00:00:58.715
And the double-angle plots of the preoperative astigmatism, the surgically induced astigmatism and the prediction error.

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:02.966
You can open any sheet of the workbook without leaving the app.

00:01:05.603 --> 00:01:16.206
This is the publication table, exactly as it is written to Excel. Each variable carries its printed label, and long cells wrap, so every group column stays in view.

00:01:16.418 --> 00:01:22.469
When you are happy with the results, save everything to your output folder, or only the files you want.

00:01:23.261 --> 00:01:27.734
StandardEyes. For ophthalmologists, by ophthalmologists.

